Ladybird keeps margins from collapsing through a box whose inline
content has a line with text on it, even at height 0. Each engine does
the same: Blink’s InlineLayoutAlgorithm resets the end margin strut
after any line that isn’t an empty line box. WebKit’s RenderBlockFlow
has childrenPreventSelfCollapsing() ask whether its inline layout
isSelfCollapsingContent(). And in Gecko, nsBlockFrame::CachedIsEmpty()
is false once any of the block’s lines isn’t empty.
